","parts":[{"text":"சாற்று","lemma":"cāṟṟu","gloss":"to cry out"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"past participle"}],"gloss":"crying out"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பெருங்கல்","parts":[{"text":"பெருமை","lemma":"perumai","gloss":"great"},{"text":"கல்","lemma":"kal","gloss":"stone/mountain"}],"gloss":"great mountain"},{"surface":"நல்","parts":[{"text":"நல்","lemma":"நல்","gloss":"good"}],"gloss":"good","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நாட்டு","parts":[{"text":"நாட்டு","lemma":"நாட்டு","gloss":"of the country"}],"gloss":"of the country","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"உமண்","parts":[{"text":"உமண்","lemma":"உமண்","gloss":"salt merchants"}],"gloss":"salt merchants","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஒலிக்குந்து","parts":[{"text":"ஒலி","lemma":"oli","gloss":"to make sound"},{"text":"க்கு","lemma":"kku","gloss":"increment"},{"text":"உந்து","lemma":"untu","gloss":"habitual participle suffix"}],"gloss":"sounding"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அன்னநன்","parts":[{"text":"அன்னநன்","lemma":"அன்னநன்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நாட்டுப்","parts":[{"text":"நாட்டுப்","lemma":"நாட்டுப்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பொருநம்","parts":[{"text":"பொருநம்","lemma":"பொருநம்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"யாமே","parts":[{"text":"யாமே","lemma":"யாமே","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"பொராஅ","parts":[{"text":"பொராஅ","lemma":"பொராஅ","gloss":"non-fighting"}],"gloss":"non-fighting","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பொருநரேம்","parts":[{"text":"பொருநரேம்","lemma":"பொருநரேம்","gloss":"we are bards"}],"gloss":"we are bards","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"குணதிசை","parts":[{"text":"குணதிசை","lemma":"குணதிசை","gloss":"eastern direction"}],"gloss":"eastern direction","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நின்று","parts":[{"text":"நின்று","lemma":"நின்று","gloss":"starting from"}],"gloss":"starting from","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"குடமுதல்","parts":[{"text":"குடம்","lemma":"kuṭam","gloss":"west"},{"text":"முதல்","lemma":"mutal","gloss":"towards"}],"gloss":"towards the west"},{"surface":"செலினும்","parts":[{"text":"செலினும்","lemma":"செலினும்","gloss":"even if it goes"}],"gloss":"even if it goes","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வடதிசை","parts":[{"text":"வடதிசை","lemma":"வடதிசை","gloss":"northern direction"}],"gloss":"northern direction","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நின்று","parts":[{"text":"நின்று","lemma":"நின்று","gloss":"starting from"}],"gloss":"starting from","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தென்வயின்","parts":[{"text":"தென்வயின்","lemma":"தென்வயின்","gloss":"towards the south"}],"gloss":"towards the south","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"செலினும்","parts":[{"text":"செலினும்","lemma":"செலினும்","gloss":"even if it goes"}],"gloss":"even if it goes","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தென்திசை","parts":[{"text":"தென்திசை","lemma":"தென்திசை","gloss":"southern direction"}],"gloss":"southern direction","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நின்று","parts":[{"text":"நின்று","lemma":"நின்று","gloss":"starting from"}],"gloss":"starting from","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"குறுகாது","parts":[{"text":"குறுகு","lemma":"kuṟuku","gloss":"to approach"},{"text":"ஆது","lemma":"ātu","gloss":"negative participle"}],"gloss":"without approaching"},{"surface":"நீடினும்","parts":[{"text":"நீடினும்","lemma":"நீடினும்","gloss":"even if it delays"}],"gloss":"even if it delays","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"யாண்டும்","parts":[{"text":"யாண்டு","lemma":"yāṇṭu","gloss":"everywhere"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"all"}],"gloss":"everywhere"},{"surface":"நிற்க","parts":[{"text":"நில்","lemma":"nil","gloss":"to stand"},{"text":"க","lemma":"ka","gloss":"optative"}],"gloss":"let it stand"},{"surface":"வெள்ளி","parts":[{"text":"வெள்ளி","lemma":"veḷḷi","gloss":"Venus star"}],"gloss":"Venus"},{"surface":"யாம்","parts":[{"text":"யாம்","lemma":"yām","gloss":"we"}],"gloss":"we"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வேண்டியது","parts":[{"text":"வேண்டியது","lemma":"வேண்டியது","gloss":"what is desired"}],"gloss":"what is desired","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"உணர்ந்தோன்","parts":[{"text":"உணர்ந்தோன்","lemma":"உணர்ந்தோன்","gloss":"he who understood"}],"gloss":"he who understood","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தாள்","parts":[{"text":"தாள்","lemma":"tāḷ","gloss":"feet/effort"}],"gloss":"feet"},{"surface":"வாழியவே","parts":[{"text":"வாழ்","lemma":"vāḻ","gloss":"to live"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"iya","gloss":"optative"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"may live long!"}]}],"literal":"Of deep water filled pond / like falling rain drops / ghee splattered fried meat to scoop / and tearing roasted meat dried meat to eat / meat containing white bowl / with cow's milk completely to wash away / sweat from eating hot food except / sweat by doing work not knowing / he who gave, my lord, his own fame to be / as for fields, fence of paddy, tall-grown sugarcane's / garden bed of many flowers blossomed having red color / as for forest land, grazing grass with many herds / is without fierce small forts of bow-residing / as for sea, wind-brought ships those who count / seashore grove's mastwood tree's branch perching low near the ground / as for salt pans, small white salt's price crying out / great mountain good country's salt merchants sounding / such good country's bards we indeed / non-fighting bards we are / from eastern direction standing even if it goes to the west / from northern direction standing even if it goes to the south / from southern direction standing even if it delays without approaching / everywhere let it stand, Venus, we / he who understood what is desired, may his feet live long!","translation":"Like the raindrops falling into a deep pond filled with water, we scoop up fried meat splattered with ghee, tear and eat roasted dried meat, and wash down the white bowls containing meat with cow's milk. Knowing no sweat from hard labor, but only the sweat of eating hot food, we sing of our lord, the giver, whose fame is his own. In his land, the fields have fences of paddy and tall sugarcane, with garden beds of many red-colored blossomed flowers. The forest lands are filled with grazing herds of cows and are free from the fierce forts of bowmen. At the sea, people count the ships brought in by the wind, while birds perch low on the branches of Punnai trees in the seashore groves. In the salt pans, salt merchants from the great mountain country cry out the price of small white salt, making a loud noise. We are the non-fighting bards of such a beautiful country. Even if the star Venus moves from east to west, or from north to south, or delays in the south without moving, we do not worry. May the feet of our king, who understands and grants what we desire, live long!","modern":"நிறைந்த நீரையுடைய ஆழமான குளத்தில் விழும் மழைத்துளிகளைப் போல, நெய் தெறிக்கும் வறுத்த இறைச்சியை அள்ளி, சுட்ட உலர்ந்த இறைச்சியைக் கிழித்து உண்டு, இறைச்சி வைத்திருந்த வெள்ளிய பாத்திரங்களைப் பசுவின் பாலால் கழுவி உண்கிறோம். உழைப்பினால் வரும் வியர்வையை அறியாமல், சூடான உணவை உண்பதால் வரும் வியர்வையை மட்டுமே உடைய எமக்குக் கொடையளித்த எம் தலைவனுடைய புகழ் நிலைப்பதாக. அவனது நாட்டில், நெல்லும் கரும்பும் வேலியாக அமைந்துள்ளன; பாத்திகளில் பல சிவந்த மலர்கள் பூத்துள்ளன. காடுகளில் பசுக்கூட்டங்கள் மேய்கின்றன; வில்லேந்திய வீரர்களின் கொடிய அரண்கள் அங்கு இல்லை. கடலில் காற்றினால் வரும் கப்பல்களை மக்கள் எண்ணுகின்றனர்; கடற்கரைச் சோலையிலுள்ள புன்னை மரக் கிளைகளில் பறவைகள் தாழ்ந்து அமர்கின்றன. உப்பங்கழிகளில், மலைநாட்டிலிருந்து வந்த உமணர்கள் வெண்மையான உப்பின் விலையைக் கூறி ஒலிக்கின்றனர். இத்தகைய வளமான நாட்டின் பாணர்கள் நாங்கள். போர் செய்யாத பாணர்கள் நாங்கள். வெள்ளி முளைக்கும் திசை மாறினாலும், எத்திசையில் நின்றாலும் எங்களுக்குக் கவலையில்லை. எமது தேவையை அறிந்து கொடுக்கும் எம் மன்னனின் திருவடிகள் வாழ்க!","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Padan tinai (praise of a king's virtues and power) and is addressed to the Chola king Killivalavan by the poet Kovur Kizhar. The poet describes the luxurious life of the bards under the king's patronage, where they feast on rich meat and milk, experiencing only the sweat of eating hot food rather than the sweat of labor. He then paints a vivid picture of the Chola kingdom's prosperity across different landscapes: the fertile agricultural fields (marutham), the peaceful forest pastures (mullai) free of bandit forts, the bustling seashore (neithal) with ships and salt merchants, and the mountain trade routes (kurinji). The poet declares that even if the star Venus (Velli) wanders from its regular path, signaling drought, the king's subjects will never suffer because of his boundless generosity. The key words include 'eethon' (he who gave), 'poyya' (unfailing), and 'vazhiya' (may he live long).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.8],[0.8,0.9],[0.9,1.5],[1.5,2.1],[2.1,2.3],[2.3,2.6],[2.6,3.0],[3.0,4.07],[4.13,4.2],[4.3,4.6],[4.6,5.1],[5.1,5.8],[5.85,6.2],[6.44,6.56],[6.56,7.2],[7.47,8.0],[8.0,8.3],[8.3,8.6],[8.6,8.6],[8.6,9.3],[9.45,9.9],[9.9,10.05],[10.05,10.5],[10.5,11.3],[11.3,11.5],[11.5,11.6],[11.6,12.0],[12.0,12.9],[12.9,13.3],[13.3,13.4],[13.4,13.8],[14.97,15.5],[15.5,15.8],[15.8,16.4],[16.5,16.6],[16.6,17.1],[17.1,17.2],[17.2,17.8],[17.8,18.1],[18.1,18.6],[18.6,19.3],[19.3,19.8],[19.8,20.3],[20.3,20.6],[20.6,20.72],[20.72,20.72],[20.72,21.22],[21.22,22.35],[22.47,22.6],[22.6,22.9],[22.9,24.1],[24.1,24.58],[24.58,25.3],[25.3,26.3],[26.3,26.6],[26.6,27.6],[27.6,27.92],[27.92,28.78],[28.84,28.9],[28.9,29.8],[29.8,30.2],[30.2,30.6],[30.6,30.8],[30.8,31.0],[32.12,32.72],[32.72,32.92],[32.92,33.85],[33.85,34.12],[34.12,35.12],[35.12,35.61],[35.61,35.92],[35.92,36.32],[36.49,36.65],[36.65,36.82],[36.82,37.35],[37.35,37.62],[37.62,38.92],[38.92,39.22],[39.22,39.79],[39.79,40.22],[40.22,41.32],[41.32,41.42],[41.42,41.78],[41.95,42.22],[42.22,43.52],[43.52,43.82],[43.82,44.22],[44.22,44.52],[44.52,45.72],[45.72,4